 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Precision:** The bit-shifting formula assumes `entry.X` fits in 14 bits (since $2^{18}$ is the shift), `entry.Y` fits in 9 bits, and `entry.Z` fits in 9 bits. If coordinates exceed these ranges, the ID computation will collide. [S1, unofficial]
-*   **Boundaries:** The source code checks for `ushort` limits in voxel space, but the directory texture format must align with the bit-packing assumptions. [S1, unofficial]
-*   **Degenerate Input:** If `directory_texture` is null, the method should skip Step 2 and 3, or handle an empty array gracefully. [S1, unofficial]
+*   **Precision:** The bit-shifting formula `((uint)entry.X << 18) | ((uint)entry.Y << 9) | (uint)entry.Z` implies `entry.X` uses 14 bits (range 0–16383), `entry.Y` uses 9 bits (range 0–511), and `entry.Z` uses 9 bits (range 0–511) [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Directory Format:** The directory texture must store entries in the exact order expected by the iteration loop, as the texture array is built sequentially from directory order [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Missing Textures:** If a computed `segment_id` has no corresponding texture in the pool, it is skipped during the rebuild [S1, unofficial].
 
